# Intent: Reset on the device (owner request 2026-11-15, docs/design/features.md "Reset the device"). Quick settings gets a Reset button that opens a screen saying in plain words what will be erased (saved Wi-Fi networks, pairing, settings) and erases nothing until its button is held for 3 seconds; Cancel or letting go early changes nothing. The clear is one repeatable step that ends in setup mode and is never half-done: a pending mark is committed first, every flash namespace except the head calibration, the radio calibration and the mark is erased, the mark is removed last, and a power loss anywhere in it is finished on the next start before any setting is read. Only the on-screen hold starts it: no tool, host command or setting calls it. It logs one local line. No resident cost: no task, timer or buffer exists until the screen is open or a reset runs; the code is flash only. English and Spanish text (the built-in font has no accents, so the Spanish is written without them). Kconfig switch MAIPAI_RESET_ON_DEVICE, default y, so the core build has it on.
# Placement: unit (a basic the robot must do alone; it runs on the screen with the host off)
# Upstream: main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc and main/hal/hal.cpp of the M5Stack StackChan firmware (MIT); the other files are new
# Check after a flash: quick settings, Reset, Cancel: nothing changes. Reset, hold 2 s and let go: nothing changes. Hold 3 s: one log line "reset done", the unit restarts into Wi-Fi setup with no saved network and no pairing. Cut power during the clear: the next start logs "a reset was interrupted: finishing it now" and ends in setup.
